# Policy: add an entry here only when a CVE has no fix available in the base
# image AND is provably unreachable from this application. Always include the
# reasoning and an `exp:` date, and prefer bumping the base image over adding
# an exception -- exceptions expire and break the deploy pipeline.

# zlib (system zlib1g 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+b1), fixed in Debian
# 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+deb13u1, waiting for
# gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian13 to pick it up.
# Unreachable: /nodejs/bin/node does not link libz (DT_NEEDED is only libc,
# libstdc++, libm, libgcc_s, libdl, libpthread) -- it statically bundles its
# own zlib 1.3.2.1 -- and node is the only process in the image.
# CVE-2026-85091: heap buffer overflow in gz_vacate() (HIGH)
CVE-2026-85091 exp:2026-11-22
# CVE-2026-76844: zlib1g (HIGH)
CVE-2026-76844 exp:2026-11-22
